# <type>(<optional scope>): <short summary, imperative, no period, ≤50 chars>
#
# <body: what changed and WHY, wrapped at 72 chars; optional for small changes>
#
# <footer: BREAKING CHANGE: ..., Refs #123, Co-Authored-By: ...>
#
# Types:
#   feat      new feature for the user
#   fix       bug fix
#   refactor  code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature
#   style     visual/UI styling changes (colours, fonts, spacing)
#   docs      documentation only (README, comments)
#   test      adding or updating tests
#   chore     tooling, config, dependencies, project settings
#   perf      performance improvement
#
# Scopes (optional): ui, data, model, logic, project
#
# Examples:
#   feat(data): store names in SwiftData
#   fix(ui): prevent adding empty names
#   refactor(logic): move duplicate check into view model
#
# Lines starting with '#' are ignored.
